# POISONED FIXTURE unit 4 of 6 — expected outcome: TIMEOUT (UNVERIFIED, not a failure)
#
# This one IS real in the sense that matters: the harness gives the unit a short
# per-unit budget and the unit genuinely outruns it (`sh -c 'sleep 30'` under a
# 1s budget), so the supervisor really does kill a really-overrunning child.
#
# The classification rule being pinned: a unit killed on its own budget is
# TIMEOUT regardless of WHICH signal enforced the budget. `timed_out` wins over
# the wait status, so a SIGKILL used to enforce a deadline must NOT be reported
# as CRASHED(137). And TIMEOUT is UNVERIFIED — it is excluded from
# failure_count(), because a unit that was never given time to answer has not
# been judged.

fn slow_unit_four(n: i64) -> i64:
    n * 4
